               "headline":  "Record sales collide with export probes; SMCI sinks to oversold near 52-week low",
               "summary":  "Super Micro closed at $21.65 on 20 Nov 2026, down 9.19% on the day and 19.4% for the week. Business results were strong: on 3 Nov it reported fiscal Q1 sales of $19.9B, almost four times a year earlier, and raised FY2027 guidance to $72–82B. The stock still fell. On 12 Nov, reports said the Justice Department is examining alleged smuggling of Supermicro servers to China, and turmoil at Nvidia dragged on AI hardware stocks. The selling is about legal risk and thin margins, not demand. The chart is firmly bearish but oversold.",
